-- title:
--   Twisting the dual preserves vanishing of archimedean H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field, let $S$ be a finite set of prime numbers, let $M$ be a finite-dimensional $k$-linear representation of the absolute Galois group $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, realised as the group of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and let $\chi$ be a homomorphism from that group to $k^\times$. The local datum `extArithLoc S` at the index `Sum.inl ()` is `archimedeanLoc`, the inclusion of the subgroup `archimedeanDecomposition` of the absolute Galois group (the archimedean member of the datum) into that group; restriction along it is the restriction of a representation to this subgroup. Assume that $H^1$ of the restriction of $M$ to `archimedeanDecomposition` is a subsingleton. Then the same holds for the restriction of `M.dualTwist χ`, the representation on the $k$-linear dual of $M$ whose action of $g$ is $\chi(g)$ times the dual action of $g$. No hypothesis on the characteristic of $k$, on $\chi$, or on $S$ is imposed; the conclusion is independent of $S$.
--
--   This is the transfer of the vanishing of the first cohomology of the decomposition group at the real place (generated by complex conjugation) from a Galois module to every character twist of its dual, a step in the bookkeeping of local terms in the Greenberg–Wiles formula. It is used by [`groupCohomology.greenbergWilesLeAdm_extArithLoc_of_isTheta1_eval_of_ne_two`](thm.html#groupCohomology.greenbergWilesLeAdm_extArithLoc_of_isTheta1_eval_of_ne_two) and [`groupCohomology.greenbergWiles_eq_unramifiedMenu_extArithLoc`](thm.html#groupCohomology.greenbergWiles_eq_unramifiedMenu_extArithLoc).
